          "Financial statements reflect a snapshot of corporate health at the balance sheet date, but commercial reality does not freeze on March 31. Standard on Auditing (SA) 560 and Ind AS 10 govern the critical window of subsequent events, establishing the auditor's active and passive responsibilities across the entire timeline from balance sheet date to the issuance and publication of the annual report.",
          "In statutory auditing and forensic assurance, the auditor's legal and professional responsibilities under Standards on Auditing (SAs) require unyielding professional skepticism and rigorous quantitative corroboration. Under Section 143 of the Companies Act, 2013, the auditor serves as an independent guardian of public trust, verifying that corporate financial statements present a true and fair view free from material misstatement whether caused by fraud or error. Every audit assertion must be substantiated with sufficient appropriate audit evidence under SA 500.",
          "In statutory auditing and forensic assurance, the auditor's legal and professional responsibilities under Standards on Auditing (SAs) require unyielding professional skepticism and rigorous quantitative corroboration. Under Section 143 of the Companies Act, 2013, the auditor serves as an independent guardian of public trust, verifying that corporate financial statements present a true and fair view free from material misstatement whether caused by fraud or error. Every audit assertion must be substantiated with sufficient appropriate audit evidence under SA 500."
